The 429 responses in this issue occur on `push` events. The only webhook subscribed to `push` was `webhook_001`, the push notification hook created in October 2024. I've removed it.

The Slack integration (`webhook_003`) isn't subscribed to `push`. It only listens to `pull_request` and `issues` events, so I left it as is. The deployment webhook (`webhook_002`) also wasn't touched.

@carlos-mendez @erik-hoffman, could you push a few commits in quick succession and check whether the 429s have stopped? If push notifications are still needed, we can re-create the hook with rate limiting or batching on the receiving end.

